# A cassette is compared byte for byte on replay, and the scripts here carry a
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang. A checkout on Windows applies core.autocrlf and
# rewrites every text file to CRLF, which breaks both: a recorded body no longer
# matches what the client sent, and executing a script fails with
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# which names the interpreter rather than the script, and so reads as though the
# script itself were missing.
#
# text=auto still lets git detect and leave binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
